course: dictionary
lesson: 595
title: One word, three jobs: average
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one you need. «Napoleon was about average height for a Frenchman of his time.» Here average means usual or ordinary, not special.
explain: Average can also be a number. The average, or mean, is what you get when you share a total equally. Add the numbers, then divide by how many there are. Add 2, 4 and 6 to get 12, then divide by 3: the average is 4.
explain: As a verb, to average is to have a certain average. «He averages 10 points a game» means that, added up and shared out over his games, his points come to 10 a game. Check which job the word is doing by reading the sentence around it.
fact: Average means usual or ordinary, not special.
fact: The average (mean) is the total divided by how many numbers there are.
fact: To find an average, add the numbers, then divide by how many there are.
fact: «On average» means over many times or many people, what usually happens.
fact: «Caesar's Julian calendar, from 45 BC, had 365 days and a leap day every 4 years, so its average year was 365 days and 6 hours.»
fact: «Gambling companies are set up so that, on average, players lose more than they win.»
exercise: «Napoleon was about average height for a Frenchman of his time.» What does average mean here? | *Usual, ordinary and not special | Very tall | Mixed up with inches | Very short
exercise: Add 2, 4 and 6, then divide by 3. What is the average (mean)? | *4 | 3 | 12 | 6
exercise: «He averages 10 points a game.» What does averages mean here? | Scores 10 points in one game only | Gives 10 points to each team | *Has an average of 10 points a game | Counts the points on a card
test: Why is Caesar's average year not exactly 365 days? | Because it always had 366 days | Because Caesar was often late | *Because a leap day every 4 years adds extra time | Because it had no days at all
test: «Gambling companies are set up so that, on average, players lose more than they win.» What does on average mean here? | *Usually, when you look at many players and games | Never, not at all | Only for horses and scratchcards | Only once, in one lucky game
exam: Tom scored 3, 5 and 10 points in three games. What is his average score? | 18 | *6 | 7 | 5
